# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-template-option -- start the CAD session from a drawing made from a given template
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: feature
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-24

* Context

alfe always hands the CAD a drawing: a per-run copy of the committed
autolisp-front-end/source/empty.dwg (without a document BricsCAD segfaults
and AutoCAD has nowhere to send the keystrokes; a fresh copy per run avoids
the "already in use, open read-only?" modal). The probe harness does the same
(probes/scripts/run-probes.sh, __DRAWING_FILE__).

empty.dwg was written by a French AutoCAD 2005 (its LAYOUT objects still
name ...\AutoCAD 2005\R16.1\enu\plotters\...): a session therefore starts on
THAT file's database -- its named-object dictionary, its styles, its layouts
("Presentation1"), metric units -- plus whatever the CAD adds when it opens
it. It is not what the CAD's own new drawing contains. That is what the
entget-pointers probe, section 12, measured for cador's default objects
(deferred-nod-default-contents): the contents of empty.dwg, not of acad.dwt.

pjb (2026-10-24): imperial and other templates are installed on the
runners; a drawing passed in avoids the units dialog a new session asks.

* Proposal

alfe --template NAME|PATH: instead of empty.dwg, copy the template (a .dwt)
into alfe's run directory as the session's drawing.

- NAME is looked up where the product keeps its templates: AutoCAD's
  Options > Files > Template Settings (TemplateDwgPath; on the Windows
  runner %LOCALAPPDATA%\Autodesk\AutoCAD <ver>\R<rel>\<lang>\Template),
  BricsCAD's templates folder (%APPDATA%\Bricsys\BricsCAD\V<nn>x64\<locale>\
  Templates; ~/Library/Application Support/Bricsys/... on macOS); a PATH is
  used as given.
- The copy keeps the per-run rule (no lock dialogs); it is opened as a
  drawing (a .dwt and a .dwg share the format), so the CAD does not prompt for
  units.
- An unknown NAME fails with the templates found listed (exit EX_NOINPUT).
- --template default: the product's own default template (AutoCAD's QNEW
  template / acad.dwt or acadiso.dwt by MEASUREINIT; BricsCAD's BASEFILE).
- Documented in the alfe manual; the probe harness passes it through
  (PROBE_TEMPLATE) so a probe can measure a new drawing of a given template.

* Acceptance

- alfe --template acad.dwt runs a script on a drawing whose MEASUREMENT is 0
  and whose ACAD_LAYOUT holds the template's layouts; acadiso.dwt gives 1.
- Both products, Windows and macOS runners; the default (no option) is
  unchanged.
